---
import MainLayout from '../layouts/MainLayout.astro';
import Section from '../components/ui/Section.astro';
import Button from '../components/ui/Button.astro';
const metrics=[['Website inquiries','18','Accepted form requests','Website form provider'],['Website call clicks','24','Taps on the phone link; not confirmed calls','Website analytics, where allowed'],['Google profile website clicks','42','Clicks from the profile to the website','Google Business Profile'],['Google profile call clicks','31','Clicks on the call button; not answered calls','Google Business Profile']];
---
<MainLayout title="Sample Monthly Report | Hometown Boost" description="See an illustrative monthly website and Google Business Profile report: the work completed, measured actions, and next priorities." quiet robots="noindex,follow">
  <Section eyebrow="A CLEAR VIEW OF THE MONTH"><h1 style="margin:0 0 30px">What your monthly report helps you see.</h1><p class="sample-notice"><strong>Illustrative sample.</strong> All numbers and business details below are invented to demonstrate the report format. They are not client results or a prediction.</p><div class="report-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">SAMPLE SERVICE BUSINESS</span><h2>Monthly website & Google review</h2></div><span class="pill">Example month</span></div><div class="report-metrics">{metrics.map(([label,value,definition,source])=><article class="card"><h3>{label}</h3><strong class="report-number">{value}</strong><p>{definition}</p><p class="note">Source: {source}</p></article>)}</div></Section>
  <Section variant="light"><div class="grid grid--3"><article class="card"><h3>Work completed</h3><ul><li>Updated seasonal service details and photos.</li><li>Published two Google profile posts.</li><li>Checked hours and review responses.</li><li>Sent the agreed review requests.</li></ul></article><article class="card"><h3>What we learned</h3><p>In this example, the main service page generated most website inquiries. Call clicks show interest, but the owner’s follow-up records are needed to identify real conversations and booked jobs.</p></article><article class="card"><h3>Next priority</h3><p>Make the quote-request step clearer on the main service page and check the result next month. Larger page builds are planned within the selected scope.</p></article></div><p class="report-note">We show unavailable data as unavailable. Website and Google profile actions can overlap, so they are not added together and presented as unique leads. Customer outcomes depend on confirmed follow-up records.</p></Section>
  <Section><div class="split"><div><h2>Connect and Local Marketing add context.</h2><p style="margin-top:20px">Connect can show inquiry sources and customer status when the connected tools support it. Local Marketing adds campaign spend, campaign actions, and landing-page work. Any cost-per-lead calculation uses a clearly stated conversion definition.</p></div><div><p>The useful question is what to do next. Each report pairs the available numbers with completed work and a practical next priority.</p><Button href="/contact/">Talk about my business ↗</Button></div></div></Section>
</MainLayout>
<style>.sample-notice{padding:20px;background:#fff3dc;border:1px solid #e6d2a9;border-radius:12px;margin:0 0 36px;max-width:900px}.report-heading{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:20px;margin-bottom:30px}.report-heading h2{font-size:1.6rem;margin-top:12px}.report-metrics{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,minmax(0,1fr));gap:18px}.report-metrics h3{font-size:1rem}.report-number{display:block;font-size:3rem;color:#174b76;margin:14px 0}.report-note{max-width:880px;margin-top:26px}ul{padding-left:20px}li{margin:10px 0}@media(max-width:980px){.report-metrics{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}}@media(max-width:560px){.report-heading{display:block}.report-heading .pill{margin-top:16px}.report-metrics{grid-template-columns:1fr}}</style>
